<title>USA: Georgetown County, S.C. to vote on $109.6 mln GOs.</title>
<headline>Georgetown County, S.C. to vote on $109.6 mln GOs.</headline>
<dateline>GEORGETOWN, S.C. 1996-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Carolina's Georgetown County has set a Sept. 20 referendum on $109.6 million of general obligation bonds for school construction, a school official said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The county school board unanimously approved the referendum Monday night despite concerns about voter support.</p>
<p>In May, voters rejected a $107.6 million school bond proposal by a margin of nearly 2-1.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
